Z||000026||Loki||08-26-2001||09:26 PM||||OK heres the engine form the 86 SE I picked up saturday morning...<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/engine.JPG"> <P>Just washed it off   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Still wet<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/loki_sig.jpg">  <BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>http://members.home.net/loki-mg||||reg||1
Z||000027||Tigger||08-26-2001||11:36 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger25before_1.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger25after_3.jpg">    <BR>Not the cleanest and not yet finished, a lot better tho...<P>Gunk degreaser on the engine and power washed the trunk carpet with 409.  I haven't tried it yet, but I've heard some good things about stuff called CD2 engine cleaner and brightener.  I usually clean or wipe down the engine before shows, sometimes at shows.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000028||Standard||08-27-2001||12:40 AM||||I've been getting at it with some wd-40 and a toothbrush, Mother's Mag & Aluminum polish on the shiny parts, it cleaned up some discoloration on the exhaust manifold coating and shined up the coolant tank real nice.  I need to pull off the IDI cover and shine up the shiny parts better, and clean up the cam housings.||||reg||1
Z||000029||MikeSchaefer||08-27-2001||06:21 AM||||Here's the engine of my 84 "hybrid", it's kinda cool.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new8engine.jpg"> <BR>  I've used a lot of cleaning stuff, and I like the gunk products the best, followed by a ton of son of a gun, to make it nice and shiny.  Yeah use a good chrome/metal polish on any metal you can see in there, it can really work wonders.  Get a nice long wire brush to save your back.  I usually just put a little piece of plastic wrap over the distributor  and then blast away with cleaning products and water, then remove the plastic quickly and run the engine to dry it off.  I've only had one time that I screwed something up in there, and it was because I neglected to cover the distributor. <BR>Cleaning your engine is a lot of fun once you have done it a few times.<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000030||MD_Fiero||08-27-2001||11:35 AM||||ok...thanks guys =)...i dont have access to my powerwasher right now(uncle has it, for his new deck)...is their anywayz i could use a water hose...and gunk engine cleaner stuff?..<P><BR>what kinda brushes should i use for what type of cleaners?<BR>gunk remover,<BR>metal/silver cleaner...etc...?<P>thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000031||Hartz||08-27-2001||12:22 PM||||I use Gunk degreaser for the heavy stuff, Simple Green for the dusty parts, and little Armor All here and there.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine2.JPG"> <P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>||||reg||1
