Z||000036||MinnGreenGT||08-28-2001||10:38 AM||||As for cleaning, my engine gets powerwashed every now and then- when necessary.  The plenum and strut tower brace are from Darrel Morse, so they have new powdercoating/paint.  I do ocassionally use a 3M "Cleaner Wax" on the plenum to get the red color back (it fades if I need to use engine degreaser).  Someone asked about the vinyl trunk cover... it came from Harry at: <A HREF="http://ourworld-top.cs.com/fiero4ever1/myhomepage/business.html" TARGET=_blank>http://ourworld-top.cs.com/fiero4ever1/myhomepage/business.html</A> He's great to work with and also has sunroof covers, sunroof bags, and matching headliner kits.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/strut1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
