Z||000077||Fierobsessed||12-16-2001||04:35 PM||||my engine is directly out of a 89 Grand Prix LE, nothing on the engine is really modified, except I surfaced the top of the plenum to remove the 3.1 multiport FI, it was upside down. I also never even bothered to separate the overdrive automatic transmission from the engine, just put it in with the motor. Now I have a ratty (This car was free, and so was the totaled Grand Prix)Fiero that still has the 2m4 decal and 13" alloys from some Oldsmobile, single exhaust, yet is as fast maybe a little quicker even than any stock v6 Fiero, the car still weighs 2660 even, 1530 on the rear 1130 on the front. It is reliable, and gets awesome highway gas mileage, and sounds great. For $400 total cost, including the grand am front brake upgrade, I think it was worth all the effort.<P>------------------<BR>Matt D<BR>1984 Indy Fiero (auto)<BR>1985 2m4 V6 DIS 3.1 Auto||||reg||11
